OS (e.g. Windows, Linux, MacOS) > RTOS (e.g FreeRTOS, )
RTOS (Real-time OS)- to ensure tasks execute w/in predictable timing
*Determinism not speed/fast
*Normal OS- best effort timing
*Types of Real-time systems- Hard (missing deadline is unacceptable, e.g. aircraft control & brake) vs 
    *Soft (occasional missed deadlines are acceptable, e.g. streaming&gaming) vs 
    *Firm (late results have no value but occasional misses are tolerable, e.g. sensor sampling)

RTOS (e.g. FreeRTOS) typically provides- 
*Task management&scheduling
*Prio
*Preemption- 
*Interrupt handling
*Timers vs Counters
*Queues, Semaphores (& Notifs?), Mutexes (if 2 tasks want the same thing), Event Groups
*Mem management

FreeRTOS- APIs..., built into ESP-IDF so no need to install separately
*vs Bare Metal (everything runs in 1 loop, simple&small but blocking & harder to scale)

BT Classic (e.g. SPP)
